{"seed":{"mim":"615425","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"EPIDERMOLYSIS BULLOSA SIMPLEX 3, LOCALIZED OR GENERALIZED INTERMEDIATE, WITH BP230 DEFICIENCY","alt_titles":[],"symbol":"EBS3","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2021},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"EPIDERMOLYSIS BULLOSA SIMPLEX 3, LOCALIZED OR GENERALIZED INTERMEDIATE, WITH BP230 DEFICIENCY","mim":"615425","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:33471381","type":"Paper","label":"Ganani et al. (2021)","pmid":"33471381","year":2021,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Epidermolysis bullosa simplex due to bi-allelic DST mutations: Case series and review of the literature."},{"id":"paper:22113475","type":"Paper","label":"Liu et al. (2012)","pmid":"22113475","year":2012,"content_level":"title","relevance":"primary","title":"Autosomal recessive epidermolysis bullosa simplex due to loss of BPAG1-e expression."},{"id":"paper:20164846","type":"Paper","label":"Groves et al. (2010)","pmid":"20164846","year":2010,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"A homozygous nonsense mutation within the dystonin gene coding for the coiled-coil domain of the epithelial isoform of BPAG1 underlies a new subtype of autosomal recessive epidermolysis bullosa simplex."},{"id":"finding:20164846:1","type":"Finding","label":"Groves et al. (2010) reported a 38-year-old man with an inherited skin fragility disorder who had lifelong generalized trauma-induced spontaneous blisters and erosions, particularly around the ankles. From age 37 years he experienced episodic numbness in his limbs; he also had a concomitant diagnosis of CADASIL, which the authors noted complicated interpretation of whether the neurologic symptoms were due to the DST mutation.","pmid":"20164846","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:DST","type":"Gene","label":"DST"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008066","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal blistering of the skin","hpo_id":"HP:0008066"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0200041","type":"Phenotype","label":"Skin erosion","hpo_id":"HP:0200041"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0033748","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hypoesthesia","hpo_id":"HP:0033748"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:20164846:2","type":"Finding","label":"In a 38-year-old man with autosomal recessive epidermolysis bullosa simplex, Groves et al. (2010) identified a homozygous nonsense mutation, p.Gln1124X, in the DST gene within the region encoding the coiled-coil domain of the epithelial isoform BPAG1-e (BP230). The authors concluded that BPAG1-e pathology underlies a new form of autosomal recessive EBS.","pmid":"20164846","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:DST:p.Q1124*","type":"Variant","label":"DST p.Q1124*","gene":"DST","keys":["p.Q1124*"],"omim_name":"DST, GLN1124TER"},{"id":"finding:20164846:3","type":"Finding","label":"Groves et al. (2010) found that the DST p.Gln1124X mutation led to loss of hemidesmosomal inner plaques and complete absence of skin immunostaining for BPAG1-e, with reduced labeling for plectin, beta-4 integrin, and type XVII collagen.","pmid":"20164846","section":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0032449","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal dermoepidermal hemidesmosome morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0032449"},{"id":"finding:22113475:1","type":"Finding","label":"Liu et al. (2012) reported autosomal recessive epidermolysis bullosa simplex caused by loss of BPAG1-e expression.","pmid":"22113475","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0007585","type":"Phenotype","label":"Skin fragility with non-scarring blistering","hpo_id":"HP:0007585"},{"id":"finding:33471381:1","type":"Finding","label":"Ganani et al. (2021) used whole-exome and direct sequencing to identify biallelic DST mutations in 5 patients with epidermolysis bullosa simplex from 3 families. Two of the variants had not been reported before: c.7097dupA (p.Tyr2366X) and c.7429delC (p.Leu2477Serfs*13).","pmid":"33471381","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:DST:c.7097dupa","type":"Variant","label":"DST c.7097dupa / p.Y2366*","gene":"DST","keys":["c.7097dupa","p.Y2366*"],"omim_name":"DST, TYR2366TER"},{"id":"variant:DST:c.7429delc","type":"Variant","label":"DST c.7429delc / p.L2477S","gene":"DST","keys":["c.7429delc","p.L2477S"],"omim_name":"DST, LEU2477SER"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001030","type":"Phenotype","label":"Fragile skin","hpo_id":"HP:0001030"},{"id":"finding:33471381:2","type":"Finding","label":"Ganani et al. (2021) reviewed 6 previously reported cases, bringing the total number of individuals with EBS due to DST variants to 11. They noted that patients displayed distinctive phenotypes regardless of the causative variant.","pmid":"33471381","section":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"finding:33471381:3","type":"Finding","label":"Ganani et al. (2021) stated that DST-associated EBS is transmitted as an autosomal recessive trait and is caused by mutations in DST, which encodes an epithelial isoform of dystonin.","pmid":"33471381","section":"inheritance"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:20164846","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:20164846:1"},{"src":"finding:20164846:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:20164846:1","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:DST","pmid":"20164846"},{"src":"finding:20164846:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0008066","pmid":"20164846","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"generalized trauma-induced blisters"},{"src":"finding:20164846:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0200041","pmid":"20164846","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"skin erosions, particularly around ankles"},{"src":"finding:20164846:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0033748","pmid":"20164846","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"episodic limb numbness"},{"src":"finding:20164846:1","rel":"asserts_inheritance","dst":"inh:AR","pmid":"20164846"},{"src":"paper:20164846","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:20164846:2"},{"src":"finding:20164846:2","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:molecular_genetics"},{"src":"finding:20164846:2","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:DST","pmid":"20164846"},{"src":"finding:20164846:2","rel":"reports_variant","dst":"variant:DST:p.Q1124*","pmid":"20164846","zygosity":"homozygous","origin":"inherited","as_reported":"p.Gln1124X"},{"src":"variant:DST:p.Q1124*","rel":"in_gene","dst":"gene:DST"},{"src":"finding:20164846:2","rel":"asserts_inheritance","dst":"inh:AR","pmi